WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
video file & English subtitles: Safex

00:00:07.041 --> 00:00:11.444
Kind-hearted as always, Candy
saves a the life of a little girl.

00:00:16.417 --> 00:00:19.777
On the train,
Candy meets a boy called Gill.

00:00:19.927 --> 00:00:23.947
Now, they continue their journey
to Florida.

00:00:25.393 --> 00:00:31.354
A beautiful rival.

00:00:49.917 --> 00:00:52.849
Look, Gill, an orange orchard!

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:59.784
We can reach them with our hands!

00:01:00.461 --> 00:01:03.021
Gill, are you ok?

00:01:03.398 --> 00:01:05.762
You put such passion in your job!

00:01:06.534 --> 00:01:07.865
But...

00:01:08.502 --> 00:01:09.895
I am so jealous of you!

00:01:10.045 --> 00:01:10.796
Why?

00:01:10.946 --> 00:01:14.602
You can head back to Chicago
as soon as you delivered the documents

00:01:15.976 --> 00:01:20.375
and meet up with your boyfriend
on Broadway.

00:01:21.482 --> 00:01:22.708
Gill...

00:01:22.858 --> 00:01:25.411
You have nothing to worry about.

00:01:25.561 --> 00:01:26.646
Gill...

00:01:27.488 --> 00:01:30.355
But I can't go back to Chicago.

00:01:30.624 --> 00:01:33.252
I am just seeking help from people.

00:01:33.402 --> 00:01:36.922
Your uncle works in a newspaper company?

00:01:37.072 --> 00:01:38.692
That's so good for you!

00:01:39.433 --> 00:01:43.870
Gill, I was adopted when I was little.

00:01:45.739 --> 00:01:47.329
Was it hard for you?

00:01:47.508 --> 00:01:49.368
Of course it was hard for me.

00:01:49.518 --> 00:01:52.139
But I felt happy sometimes.

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:59.144
Look, Gill, the sea!

00:02:04.125 --> 00:02:07.026
It's my first time
to see such a beautiful coast.

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:12.525
I feel so good, so comfortable...

00:02:12.675 --> 00:02:14.960
Candy,

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:19.938
It's still summer in Florida!
America is so big!

00:02:58.145 --> 00:03:01.637
Here we are, safely.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:07.982
Take care, Gill.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.983
Are you going to your uncle's
by yourself?

00:03:11.133 --> 00:03:12.150
Yes.

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:13.518
Good bye.

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:19.365
Thank you for everything, Candy!

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:22.298
Be good, Gill!

00:03:25.439 --> 00:03:26.667
It's time to go.

00:03:36.283 --> 00:03:38.274
Houses here are so beautiful!

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:40.315
There are villas all over.

00:03:42.923 --> 00:03:47.087
The kids from Pony's Home
would love this place.

00:03:54.301 --> 00:03:57.270
Kurin and Mina, how are they now?

00:03:58.538 --> 00:04:02.907
Where could be principal Kreis' villa?

00:04:11.952 --> 00:04:13.817
I guess it's here.

00:04:20.594 --> 00:04:22.459
Excuse me...

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:27.432
The principal's daughter?

00:04:29.568 --> 00:04:32.659
You had a long journey,
you must be tired.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.574
Are you the principal?

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:44.410
It's nice to meet you!
I am Candice White.

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:47.677
Candy.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.028
How's it going?

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:53.183
Good and bad.

00:04:58.131 --> 00:04:59.359
Excuse me...

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:02.891
Leonard made a good decision.

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:05.496
Why is that?

00:05:05.746 --> 00:05:12.003
I asked him
to send a strong nurse here.

00:05:12.153 --> 00:05:13.739
Strong?

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:17.782
You are strong enough.

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:21.513
You should stay here for a few months.

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:23.713
That's too long.

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:26.591
You are going to like this place.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:30.127
But I need to go to Broadway
next week.

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.697
What a coincidence!

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:38.531
The patient you will be looking after
just came back from Broadway.

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:45.010
She is my relative's daughter,
she is very naughty.

00:05:58.291 --> 00:05:59.750
You are welcome.

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:01.450
Yes.

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:03.721
Did Karen eat anything?

00:06:03.871 --> 00:06:07.323
No, just some grapefruit.

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:10.765
That's not good.

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:15.630
What is wrong with her?

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:18.870
Karen doesn't need doctors
or medicine.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:20.872
She needs a friend.

00:06:21.022 --> 00:06:24.008
But just like I said...

00:06:24.158 --> 00:06:28.179
As things stand right now,
Karen might kill herself.

00:06:28.329 --> 00:06:30.948
Suicide? Why?

00:06:31.198 --> 00:06:34.001
She just won't speak.

00:06:36.329 --> 00:06:40.527
Maybe a young friend
could open her heart.

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:50.574
Karen, it's me, open the door!

00:06:51.444 --> 00:06:54.880
She stays alone in her room all day.

00:06:55.214 --> 00:06:58.706
You said she came from Broadway.

00:06:59.752 --> 00:07:04.048
Karen was an actress
in the Strasford troupe.

00:07:04.198 --> 00:07:05.750
The Strasford troupe?

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:07.952
Terry's troupe!

00:07:08.702 --> 00:07:10.219
You know about it?

00:07:11.497 --> 00:07:13.192
That's great!

00:07:14.032 --> 00:07:19.299
Karen, Candy from Chicago
heard about your troupe.

00:07:25.644 --> 00:07:28.112
- Karen.
- Uncle, don't come in.

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:30.277
- But...
- Come in.

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:40.521
Sorry to disturb you.

00:07:40.959 --> 00:07:43.189
Did uncle tell you anything?

00:07:43.662 --> 00:07:46.529
Nothing, he just thought
you might be bored.

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:49.061
Let me tell you,

00:07:50.235 --> 00:07:53.199
I am not sick at all.

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:57.040
I am just protesting silently.

00:07:57.709 --> 00:08:00.271
The Principal is worried about you.

00:08:00.421 --> 00:08:03.879
You heard about the Strasford troupe?

00:08:04.349 --> 00:08:07.375
I watched their show
at Elmore Theatre, in Chicago.

00:08:07.586 --> 00:08:08.951
King Lear.

00:08:09.988 --> 00:08:11.745
That was a bad performance.

00:08:11.995 --> 00:08:14.418
I don't know much about play.

00:08:14.568 --> 00:08:16.220
I am sure even you could tell.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:18.559
That actress didn't know how to act.

00:08:19.698 --> 00:08:21.525
Which actress?

00:08:21.775 --> 00:08:22.997
Susanna.

00:08:23.402 --> 00:08:25.336
Susanna Marlowe, of course!

00:08:26.505 --> 00:08:27.699
Susanna?

00:08:28.941 --> 00:08:32.342
An amateur playing Juliet, come on!

00:08:34.646 --> 00:08:37.080
So she was Susanna's rival.

00:08:38.684 --> 00:08:41.346
You had the same thought, right?

00:08:43.088 --> 00:08:44.515
Sit down.

00:08:44.665 --> 00:08:46.023
Thank you.

00:08:47.326 --> 00:08:50.887
Do you know the reason
why I couldn't play Juliet?

00:08:53.398 --> 00:08:57.626
Because Susanna would have done
anything to get the role.

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:01.539
Harry Grant and Susanna Marlowe.

00:09:02.374 --> 00:09:05.502
I can do better
if I work with Terrius.

00:09:06.311 --> 00:09:08.575
She is obsessed with Terrius.

00:09:08.847 --> 00:09:10.212
Terry?

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:13.678
Terry?

00:09:13.952 --> 00:09:16.978
No, Mr. Terrius.

00:09:18.189 --> 00:09:20.384
He has a bright future.

00:09:20.825 --> 00:09:22.686
I thought so too.

00:09:22.836 --> 00:09:26.492
But Susanna used him.

00:09:27.799 --> 00:09:30.666
Susanna used Terry?

00:09:30.902 --> 00:09:33.632
Would she?

00:09:42.513 --> 00:09:46.343
I could never lose to Susanna
if it were about talent.

00:09:46.585 --> 00:09:49.782
The showbiz is complicated.

00:09:50.288 --> 00:09:54.991
Sooner or later
I will show my talent to Susanna!

00:09:58.863 --> 00:10:01.024
Let's go get something to eat.

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:03.462
I...

00:10:04.102 --> 00:10:08.061
To thank you
for bearing with my complaints.

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:14.704
Karen said she wanted to eat?

00:10:15.254 --> 00:10:16.168
Yes.

00:10:17.348 --> 00:10:21.182
Great, it's so good to have you here!

00:10:21.686 --> 00:10:25.417
Principal,
I would like to go back tomorrow.

00:10:25.623 --> 00:10:27.891
You don't need to be
in so much hurry.

00:10:28.426 --> 00:10:30.152
I must go back...

00:10:30.302 --> 00:10:31.524
No.

00:10:34.098 --> 00:10:36.120
I want you to stay here for a while.

00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:38.234
Is there any problem, uncle?

00:10:39.437 --> 00:10:42.964
Candy, I will inform Leonard.

00:10:43.574 --> 00:10:44.800
What should I do?

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:47.303
I need to leave
before tomorrow noon.

00:10:47.453 --> 00:10:49.938
Otherwise, I will miss Terry's show.

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:15.097
What a nice restaurant.

00:11:20.277 --> 00:11:23.576
I know what you are thinking right now.

00:11:25.048 --> 00:11:27.642
You must be thinking about Terrius.

00:11:28.318 --> 00:11:30.377
- No.
- Stop pretending.

00:11:31.054 --> 00:11:32.954
You called him "Terry" earlier.

00:11:33.523 --> 00:11:34.983
I...

00:11:35.133 --> 00:11:38.453
You and Terry must be very close.

00:11:38.603 --> 00:11:41.326
Are you in a rush to Broadway?

00:11:41.765 --> 00:11:42.823
Karen...

00:11:45.936 --> 00:11:48.063
I think you better give up.

00:11:48.972 --> 00:11:50.065
Why?

00:11:50.215 --> 00:11:54.907
I am not against you and Terry.

00:11:55.445 --> 00:11:56.888
So why?

00:11:57.038 --> 00:12:00.108
I want Susanna to have
less audience when performing.

00:12:00.258 --> 00:12:02.048
This is not a reason!

00:12:02.386 --> 00:12:05.583
Until the show ends,
you will stay here.

00:12:06.089 --> 00:12:09.553
You will see Terry
whenever you want after that.

00:12:09.793 --> 00:12:13.957
Terry must have sent the invitation
to Chicago.

00:12:14.831 --> 00:12:17.732
I must go to Broadway tomorrow.

00:12:31.881 --> 00:12:35.574
I can't stay here
and waste my time with her.

00:12:41.391 --> 00:12:43.518
Please be quiet!

00:12:55.238 --> 00:12:56.500
Candy!

00:12:57.541 --> 00:12:59.065
Good night.

00:13:01.511 --> 00:13:03.445
Practising your tricks?

00:13:08.652 --> 00:13:12.554
What do you think?
This is Florida's fruit wine.

00:13:13.023 --> 00:13:14.483
Thank you.

00:13:14.833 --> 00:13:18.123
I didn't know
you love Terrius so much.

00:13:18.395 --> 00:13:19.955
I don't.

00:13:20.105 --> 00:13:21.490
Stop pretending.

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:25.794
I am an actress,
I saw through you straight away.

00:13:25.944 --> 00:13:29.431
Then please let me go to Broadway!

00:13:29.581 --> 00:13:33.435
I am sorry but I am afraid
Terry won't be available.

00:13:33.685 --> 00:13:35.170
Why?

00:13:35.320 --> 00:13:37.907
There is a rumour
in the Strasford troupe.

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:42.142
The actor and actress
playing Romeo and Juliet

00:13:42.292 --> 00:13:44.186
will eventually fall in love.

00:13:49.492 --> 00:13:51.052
How is that possible?

00:13:51.202 --> 00:13:52.854
Director Robert's wife.

00:13:53.004 --> 00:13:56.091
She used to play the role of Juliet.

00:13:56.241 --> 00:13:58.100
And there are others too.

00:14:01.604 --> 00:14:05.066
Terry and Susanna
have been rehearsing day and night.

00:14:05.216 --> 00:14:06.608
Stop it!

00:14:08.678 --> 00:14:12.375
We both lost to Susanna.

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:15.477
Good bye.

00:14:22.325 --> 00:14:24.020
I don't believe in rumours.

00:14:24.494 --> 00:14:27.254
I just believe Terry.

00:14:27.404 --> 00:14:29.527
Terry believes in me too.

00:14:30.266 --> 00:14:31.563
Terry...

00:14:36.673 --> 00:14:39.433
Adjust the lighting
more to the right.

00:14:39.609 --> 00:14:41.941
And focus on those two people.

00:14:44.781 --> 00:14:46.373
Let's do it again.

00:14:46.983 --> 00:14:48.917
Romeo and Juliet
come up to each other.

00:14:50.286 --> 00:14:52.720
Start from the banquet scene.

00:14:59.396 --> 00:15:01.922
O, she doth teach the torches
to burn bright!

00:15:02.072 --> 00:15:04.830
It seems she hangs
upon the cheek of night

00:15:14.843 --> 00:15:17.905
Did my heart love till now?
forswear it, sight!

00:15:18.055 --> 00:15:21.811
For I ne'er saw true beauty
till this night.

00:15:23.719 --> 00:15:28.156
Terry, watch out! Terry!

00:15:40.502 --> 00:15:41.628
Susanna!

00:15:41.803 --> 00:15:43.134
Susanna!

00:15:43.572 --> 00:15:44.732
Susanna!

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:48.009
Susanna!

00:16:10.598 --> 00:16:12.156
It's dawn.

00:16:12.367 --> 00:16:16.428
I guess Terry finished
the last rehearsal.

00:16:34.089 --> 00:16:37.422
Terry, watch out! Terry!

00:16:39.961 --> 00:16:42.896
Despite her being tiny and frail,

00:16:43.164 --> 00:16:46.292
she sacrificed herself to save me.

00:16:47.302 --> 00:16:49.566
Susanna, don't die!

00:17:02.484 --> 00:17:04.213
Candy!

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:07.149
Candy!

00:17:07.655 --> 00:17:10.215
Gill, it's you!

00:17:11.226 --> 00:17:13.386
Good morning! I will be delivering
newspapers from today onwards.

00:17:13.536 --> 00:17:15.326
So many newspapers?

00:17:16.031 --> 00:17:18.558
Right, I will help you too!

00:17:18.708 --> 00:17:20.191
Can you do it, Candy?

00:17:20.368 --> 00:17:21.835
No problem!

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:34.248
Wait for me, Candy!

00:17:34.749 --> 00:17:37.149
Quick, we can't be late!

00:17:37.886 --> 00:17:40.380
- I am relieved now.
- Why?

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:44.755
You looked upset just now,
I was worried.

00:17:45.994 --> 00:17:48.258
You look so energetic!

00:17:48.563 --> 00:17:50.793
Uncle has been good to me.

00:17:51.199 --> 00:17:52.792
Let's keep going!

00:17:52.942 --> 00:17:54.164
Ok!

00:18:17.325 --> 00:18:19.190
Doctor, Susanna...

00:18:19.928 --> 00:18:21.953
She is fine.

00:18:23.598 --> 00:18:25.122
Thank you.

00:18:26.134 --> 00:18:29.831
But her right leg...

00:18:31.239 --> 00:18:32.732
Right leg?

00:18:32.882 --> 00:18:34.601
I did my best.

00:18:34.751 --> 00:18:37.702
It needed to be amputated
for her to live.

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:40.539
Amputated?

00:18:43.118 --> 00:18:44.915
Susanna!

00:18:45.353 --> 00:18:47.014
Poor girl!

00:18:49.924 --> 00:18:53.961
Susanna was trying to save me...
She sacrificed herself for me!

00:19:06.307 --> 00:19:08.673
That's it.

00:19:10.444 --> 00:19:11.270
Thanks!

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:13.104
I was lucky to have you to help.

00:19:14.081 --> 00:19:16.106
Work hard!

00:19:17.218 --> 00:19:19.045
You going back today, Candy?

00:19:20.154 --> 00:19:22.315
I was.

00:19:23.691 --> 00:19:25.591
Are you not going back anymore?

00:19:25.793 --> 00:19:28.819
No, I have to go back.

00:19:29.363 --> 00:19:32.821
I must let them know my situation.

00:19:36.203 --> 00:19:39.661
I have confirmed the documents.

00:19:42.142 --> 00:19:45.894
I will go back to Chicago
in spring, next year.

00:19:47.181 --> 00:19:49.274
So I can go back to Chicago?

00:19:49.884 --> 00:19:53.381
Karen is fine now.

00:19:54.555 --> 00:19:55.882
Karen?

00:19:56.332 --> 00:19:59.084
She went back to New York
this morning.

00:19:59.234 --> 00:20:03.823
Come and gone.

00:20:04.073 --> 00:20:06.792
She went back to Broadway.

00:20:07.701 --> 00:20:10.169
Miss Karen? Yes.

00:20:10.571 --> 00:20:13.771
She got this morning a message
from New York.

00:20:14.081 --> 00:20:16.542
What was it about?

00:20:16.977 --> 00:20:19.872
It was maybe from her boyfriend.

00:20:20.022 --> 00:20:22.641
She looked nervous.

00:20:22.791 --> 00:20:24.115
Is that so?

00:20:47.708 --> 00:20:51.007
I am going back to Chicago
and then heading towards Broadway.

00:20:52.079 --> 00:20:54.070
I will finally meet Terry.

00:20:58.285 --> 00:21:00.661
But Candy didn't know

00:21:01.288 --> 00:21:06.116
that Karen left to replace Susanna
and perform in the show on Broadway.

00:21:08.295 --> 00:21:10.108
She has no idea.

00:21:10.797 --> 00:21:14.756
At the other end
of this warm south country,

00:21:15.702 --> 00:21:19.661
the freezing Broadway
is awaiting her visit.
